\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Day of wrath! O day of mourning!
\par See fulfilled the prophet's warning,
\par Heaven and earth to ashes burning.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O what fear man's bosom rendeth,
\par When from heaven the Judge 
\par descendeth,
\par On whose sentence all dependeth.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Wondrous sound the trumpet 
\par filingeth,
\par Through earth's sepulchres it ringeth,
\par All before the throne it bringeth.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Death is struck, and nature quaking,
\par All creation is awaking,
\par To its Judge an answer making.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Lo! The Book, exactly worded,
\par Wherein all hath been recorded;
\par Thence shall judgement be awarded.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. When the Judge His seat attaineth
\par And each hidden deed arraigneth,
\par Nothing unavenged remaineth.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7.  What shall I, frail man, be pleading,
\par Who for me be interceding,
\par When the just are mercy needing?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. King of majesty tremendous,
\par Who dost free salvation send us,
\par Fount of pity, then befriend us.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 9. Think, good Jesu, my salvation
\par Caused Thy wondrous incarnation,
\par Leave me not to reprobation.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 10\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 10. Faint and weary Thou hast 
\par sought me,
\par On the Cross of suffering bought me;
\par Shall such grace be vainly brought me?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 11\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 11. Righteous Judge; for sin's pollution,
\par Grant Thy gift of absolution,
\par Ere that day of retribution.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 12\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 12. Guilty, now I pour my moaning,
\par All my shame with anguish owning;
\par Spare, O God, Thy suppliant groaning.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 13\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 13. Thou the sinful woman savedst
\par Thou the dying thief forgavest,
\par And to me a hope vouchsafest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 14\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 14. Worthless are my prayers and sighing,
\par Yet, good Lord, in grace complying,
\par Rescue me from fires undying.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 15\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 15. With Thy favoured sheep O place me,
\par Nor among the goats abase me,
\par But to Thy right hand upraise me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 16\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 16. Low I kneel, with heart- submission;
\par See, like ashes, my contrition;
\par Help me in my last condition.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 17\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 17. Ah, that day of tears and morning!
\par from the dust of earth returning,
\par Man for judgement must prepare him.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 18\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 18. Spare, O God, in mercy spare him,
\par Lord all pitying, Jesu blest,
\par Grant us Thine eternal rest!
\par                               Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

